g></button><div class="xb3r6kr" data-projection-id="7" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div inert=""><div class="x78zum5 xdt5ytf"><div class="x78zum5 x6s0dn4 xrdokzc"><div class="x1n2onr6 x1kky2od x2lah0s xkh2ocl"><div class="x10l6tqk xxwu3sf x13vifvy x1ey2m1c xe0pwq x19ypqd9 xa0awrb"></div></div><div class="xuzfeq1 x8yk33q x1e00guj x18zpg43 x22v61l x78zum5 x6s0dn4 x1sk9g4k xeuugli xbhfabm x1iyjqo2 xlk80a5"><span class="x2lah0s">Explored</span><button data-fpl-component="primitive" type="button" tabindex="0" data-show-focus="true" class="_19xx72g0 xeuugli xb3r6kr xlyipyv xuxw1ft x1lliihq xlk80a5 x1633fg2 xkrqix3 x1sur9pj x1f2jko9">App.tsx</button></div></div><div class="x78zum5 x6s0dn4 xrdokzc"><div class="x1n2onr6 x1kky2od x2lah0s xkh2ocl"><div class="x10l6tqk xxwu3sf x13vifvy x1ey2m1c xe0pwq x19ypqd9 xa0awrb"></div></div><div class="xuzfeq1 x8yk33q x1e00guj x18zpg43 x22v61l x78zum5 x6s0dn4 x1sk9g4k xeuugli xbhfabm x1iyjqo2 xlk80a5"><span class="x2lah0s">Explored</span><button data-fpl-component="primitive" type="button" tabindex="0" data-show-focus="true" class="_19xx72g0 xeuugli xb3r6kr xlyipyv xuxw1ft x1lliihq xlk80a5 x1633fg2 xkrqix3 x1sur9pj x1f2jko9">index.css</button></div></div><div class="x78zum5 x6s0dn4 xrdokzc"><div class="x1n2onr6 x1kky2od x2lah0s xkh2ocl"><div class="x10l6tqk xxwu3sf x13vifvy x1ey2m1c xe0pwq x19ypqd9 xa0awrb"></div></div><div class="xuzfeq1 x8yk33q x1e00guj x18zpg43 x22v61l x78zum5 x6s0dn4 x1sk9g4k xeuugli xbhfabm x1iyjqo2 xlk80a5"><span class="x2lah0s">Explored</span><button data-fpl-component="primitive" type="button" tabindex="0" data-show-focus="true" class="_19xx72g0 xeuugli xb3r6kr xlyipyv xuxw1ft x1lliihq xlk80a5 x1633fg2 xkrqix3 x1sur9pj x1f2jko9">index.html</button></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="x78zum5 xdt5ytf"><div class="x78zum5 xdt5ytf"><button data-fpl-component="primitive" aria-expanded="false" type="button" tabindex="0" data-show-focus="true" class="_19xx72g0 x78zum5 x6s0dn4 xxs79tx x1o1pmfc xh8yej3 x87ps6o x11g6tue xng3xce x1717udv xdpxx8g xlk80a5 xn7s738 xt3l3uh x1j0wymg x1em0e x9lcvmn xkrqix3 x1f2jko9"><span class="xuzfeq1 x8yk33q x1e00guj x18zpg43 x22v61l">Reasoning</span><svg width="24" height="24" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" class="x2lah0s x1wt4b31 x11xpdln xbvmna6 x1em0e x9lcvmn" data-fpl-icon-size="24L"><path fill="var(--fpl-icon-color, var(--color-icon))" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10.146 16.354a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708L13.793 12l-3.647-3.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708-.708l4 4a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .708l-4 4a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button><div class="xb3r6kr" data-projection-id="8" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div inert=""><div class="xlk80a5 x889kno x1hx0egp x1odjw0f xkcv6ua x1ed109x x1597r2g xsal60d x1eazdmp"><div class="x1hx0egp x1ed109x"><p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm thinking I should build an in-app "Directions" exploration view alongside a final polished product reflecting the recommended direction, keeping it feasible as a single app with a few files. I'm leaning toward a "Writers' Room Noir" concept — editorial, cinematic, dark, with a transitional serif display font.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For typography I'm settling on Newsreader as the display serif, Hanken Grotesk for body text, DM Mono for labels, and Amiri paired with IBM Plex Sans Arabic for Arabic support. I'm sketching three distinct directions: a cinematic "Title Sequence" look with film-strip navigation and screenplay formatting, a brutalist "Specimen/Lab" look with terminal-style logs, and a warm "Atelier/Moodboard" look with a spatial canvas of floating clippings — and I'm leaning toward recommending the Title Sequence direction, possibly blending in elements from the Lab aesthetic.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm planning the overall architecture: App.tsx managing view state, language, and direction, with separate files for styles/tokens, i18n copy, data, and components including a Directions picker, a Shell for the navigation rail, and individual stage components (Home, Brief, Engines, Insight, Concept, Script, Output). I'm keeping everything frontend-only with mocked generation via fake streaming and timeouts, and I'm defining a warm dark color palette with near-black backgrounds, bone-colored ink, and muted rule lines.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm settling on vermilion as the single accent color with each AI engine getting a distinct glyph rather than its own color, and I'm setting up Tailwind v4 theming with logical CSS properties for proper RTL/LTR support tied to the dir attribute. For the i18n content, I'm sketching a demo brief around a fictional client brand to populate the English and Arabic copy.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm landing on "Dar Coffee" — a Gulf specialty roaster launching a cold brew for nighttime drinking — with an insight about coffee at night being about refusing to let the day end, and a concept called "The Second Sunset." I'm drafting the bilingual content data structure now, with a brief object and five engine entries each needing their own fields.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Still sketching the data model: insight candidates with surface/tension/opportunity framing, a concept with pillars and manifesto, and an editable scene-based script leading to a final poster-style output. I'm also defining the stage flow through brief, insight, concept, and script, with a pipeline bar tracking progress across those core stages.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Rethinking the flow, I want Engines to act as a "lens" step between Brief and Insight, so the pipeline becomes Brief → Engines (lens) → Insight → Concept → Script → Output. I'll keep the top rail showing four big stages plus Output, with the chosen lens surfaced as a persistent, clickable chip that lets the user jump back to re-select it.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Every workspace screen should share the same anatomy: a left "thinking trace" column showing the AI's reasoning (lens, assumptions, trace lines), a center editable work area, and an action bar for Regenerate/Edit/Next, all sitting under a 12-column grid with a top bar (logo, pipeline, language toggle) and a status line at the bottom showing stage progress. I'm planning a shared Stage layout component that takes props for the stage number, title, description, trace array, children, and actions, with a sticky trace column on the left. For the Engines page itself, I'm picturing five large numbered rows styled as an editorial index list rather than cards.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Hovering a row expands it to reveal how the engine works plus a sample provocation; selecting it highlights the choice, and "Run engine" triggers a loading sequence into the insight view — I'll keep selection single rather than allowing blending. On the insight page, I'm planning a short "generating" animation with trace lines appearing, followed by three large serif insight statements that are selectable via radio and editable in place. For regeneration, rather than writing a full 15-insight matrix across all engines and both languages, I'm compromising: each engine has one base set of three insights plus a short engine-specific framing line, and regenerating cycles to a second set of three.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For concepts, instead of branching off every insight combination, I'm simplifying to three fixed "routes" (A/B/C) shown as tabs, each with its own title, tagline, and manifesto that's editable, and the chosen route's title and tagline just get substituted into a shared script structure rather than writing separate scripts per route. The script itself will use fixed scenes with two voiceover alternates each for regeneration, formatted screenplay-style using a Courier-like monospace font.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For layout, I'm picturing a bone-colored paper sheet for the screenplay sitting on a dark background for contrast, with a vertical scene list on the left showing durations, the editable screenplay in the center, and a scene inspector on the right with shot suggestions, mood, duration, and a regenerate button, plus a bottom timeline strip showing all scenes proportional to a 60-second total. The final output screen splits into a 16:9 title card poster on one side and a vertical ledger on the other tracing Brief → Insight → Concept → Script with jump-back edit links and export/copy/restart buttons.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the home workspace, I'm thinking a bold "FX" title, a pipeline diagram, a list of the five engines, a recent labs table-style list, and a "Begin a new brief" CTA, plus a language toggle and recent sessions with stage progress — keeping it functional rather than marketing-like. The brief page is a structured editorial form with a big free-text area plus underlined fields for client, objective, audience, tone, and constraints, paired with a live "FX reads" panel showing detected keyword chips, tension flags, missing elements, word count, and a simulated readiness score before moving to "Choose your lens."</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For directions, I want three distinct tabs/panels each with its own mini CSS mockup covering identity, layout philosophy, navigation model, workspace structure, and script experience, each themed with unique backgrounds and fonts, followed by a recommendation panel with an "Enter FX — Direction A" button. Since exploration should come before recommendation, I'm leaning toward making directions the initial route, framed as an "Exploration" stage ahead of the main product experience.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also pinning down font pairings for each direction: Direction A uses Newsreader with Hanken Grotesk, Direction B goes brutalist with DM Mono and Archivo, and Direction C feels warm with Instrument Serif and Instrument Sans. For Arabic text, I'll pair Amiri for display in A and C with IBM Plex Sans Arabic for body copy, and consider Reem Kufi for Direction B's more brutalist feel, keeping the specimen text brief enough to just hint at the pairing.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">A broken URL would just fail that one import silently, so that's an acceptable risk. For font tokens, I'm setting up display and sans variables that swap in Amiri and IBM Plex Sans Arabic when the direction is RTL, redefining the CSS custom properties on <code class="xho5uc7 xlqn4i6 x4p5aij x1j85h84 xf00w7v x1d60ukw x15klxpg x1hjwid2 x1hlhp33">[dir="rtl"]</code> so Tailwind's theme variables cascade correctly.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I also want to kill letter-spacing and uppercase tracking on labels in RTL mode, switching to a plain sans font with zero tracking instead. For the rest I'm adding fade-up rise animations with staggered delays, a subtle SVG noise grain overlay on body::after, a custom selection color, and I'm weighing whether hiding scrollbars conflicts with the no-unlayered-resets constraint.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm planning the actual file structure: a central CSS file, a content/types file with bilingual data, an App shell handling state and routing, a shared UI components file for labels and buttons and editable text, and then separate view files for each workspace step like Home, Brief, Engines, and Script.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm designing the session state shape, deciding to keep everything in a single "work" object in App with useState, tracking things like language, chosen engine, insight selections, and scene edits, then passing that state and setter down to each view.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm thinking about language toggling: if someone switches language mid-session, do edits get wiped? Keeping a separate work object per language (<code class="xho5uc7 xlqn4i6 x4p5aij x1j85h84 xf00w7v x1d60ukw x15klxpg x1hjwid2 x1hlhp33">works: Record&lt;Lang, Work&gt;</code>) seems cleaner than resetting content on every toggle, preserving user edits while still letting locale defaults apply.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For insights, I want each Work to track its own regenerated text array plus a flag for whether generation has already happened, so re-entering a view doesn't replay the full generation animation unnecessarily -- just use local loading state tied to a mount check against that flag.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Switching engines should reset that flag though, since the insight content should feel tied to the engine. I'm leaning toward each engine contributing a couple of distinct "angle" insights plus some shared ones across sets, so different engines don't just produce identical-feeling output -- something like 10 engine-specific plus 4 shared lines total.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm drafting the bilingual script itself, titled "The Second Sunset," built around five scenes starting with dusk over Riyadh and moving into the city waking up at night—framing the idea that real life in the Gulf begins after sunset.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Scene two shows Nour closing and reopening her laptop with a quiet "Not yet," scene three focuses on the Dar Cold Brew pour in close-up amber detail, and scene four moves to a Corniche night montage of skaters, musicians, and late-night life, each with matching Arabic/English VO lines reinforcing the brand's after-dark tagline.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm finalizing the title card and naming the client "Dar" (دار), then planning the bilingual content file with trace lines, taglines, and insights for each engine, keeping the structure concise before writing it out.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm drafting the UI copy, including stage names and a pipeline rail that runs Brief → Lens → Insight → Concept → Script → Output, styling Lens as a distinct diamond-shaped node.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the home screen I'm working on a heading like "A brief goes in. A film comes out." along with sample recent labs across different stages — things like "Dar Cold Brew — The Second Sunset" at Script 78%, "Hayat Telecom — Roaming Home" at Concept, and similar entries showing progress by stage.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm setting up the color palette as theme tokens — dark ink backgrounds, bone-colored text for contrast, a faint muted tone for decorative elements, and a signal orange accent, checking contrast ratios for accessibility as I go.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also sketching shared UI components: a Label with uppercase monospace styling and RTL support, and a Btn component with square-cornered primary/ghost variants plus a flipping arrow icon for right-to-left layouts.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the editable text component, I'm using contentEditable with blur-based updates so onChange only fires once editing finishes, adding a dotted-underline hover affordance and focus outline, while confirming React can safely swap the text node if the value changes externally after a regenerate.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm structuring the Stage layout — a grid with a sidebar holding the eyebrow label, number, title, description, and a thinking trace panel, alongside a main content area for children.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Below that I'm adding a fixed ActionBar at the bottom with status fields (Editable/Regenerate/Next), a back button, and a primary Next button, plus a Trace component that animates thinking lines in sequentially with timestamps and a pulsing signal dot while active.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the top shell, I'm designing a logo mark, a horizontal pipeline rail showing step progress with mono numbering, a language toggle, and a condensed label for narrow screens. Below that I want a thin "lens chip" ribbon that surfaces the current lens, insight, and concept chain so the user always sees the AI's reasoning context.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm sketching the Home view: a hero section with a huge display headline split across two lines, a right-column blurb with primary and secondary CTAs, followed by the pipeline strip.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Below that, I'm planning four numbered columns (Brief, Insight, Concept, Script) each with a short verb phrase and a connecting line that's clickable to jump views, plus a "Lens" band listing the five engines with small glyphs, and a "In the lab" table of recent sessions. For the engine glyphs, I'm designing simple unique SVG shapes instead of emoji -- a triangle with a dot for provocation, overlapping circles for analogies, scattered dots for random, and distinct marks for the rest.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the Brief view itself, I'm sketching a stage with a "FX reads your brief" trace, a big serif textarea for the brief text, a two-column grid of underlined fields (Client, Objective, Audience, Tone, Constraint), and a left sidebar showing live trace lines plus a segmented "Brief strength" meter that fills as fields are completed.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the Engines view, I'm laying out five selectable engine rows (number, glyph, name/question, arrow), where selecting one expands to reveal "How it thinks," a provocation applied to the user's brief in big serif italic, and three strategic insight outputs, with a "Run engine →" action that navigates onward and triggers insight generation.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the Insight view, I'm planning a load sequence that shows trace animation lines over 2.4s before revealing three insights as editable serif statements labeled A/B/C with small mono tension lines, where selecting one highlights it with a signal bar while dimming the others.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the chosen insight I want to add a shared three-part scaffold underneath — surface behavior, hidden tension, opportunity — written directly into content and editable. For the Concept view, I'm structuring three route tabs with large serif titles that expand into editable headline, tagline, manifesto, and three pillars, plus a quote linking back to the source insight, with regenerate resetting the current route's edits to its default.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'll keep regenerate simple: it triggers a brief "Rewriting…" overlay, then cycles the route's tagline between two preset options rather than building a full alt-wording system. For the visual key frame, I'll avoid external images and instead build the amber sunset look purely with layered CSS radial gradients behind the big typographic title.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the "Still" component, I'm building a letterboxed panel with a gradient sky, a sun arc, and a city skyline rendered as an SVG of bars with varying heights, reused across the Home hero, Concept, Output, and Script preview frames. For the Script view layout, I'm rethinking the column split since Stage already reserves a side column, so I need a custom grid for the scene list, paper page, and inspector panels instead.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm planning a custom full-width Script layout: a 260px left rail with trace and scene filmstrip, a center paper area, a 280px right inspector, and a bottom timeline above the action bar — possibly adding a <code class="xho5uc7 xlqn4i6 x4p5aij x1j85h84 xf00w7v x1d60ukw x15klxpg x1hjwid2 x1hlhp33">wide</code> prop to Stage to skip its default aside, while reusing ActionBar and Trace components. The paper itself will show the full screenplay continuously across all scenes in proper screenplay formatting (slug lines, action, character, dialogue, V.O.), with the selected scene highlighted and scrollIntoView used for navigation, styled in Courier Prime on an aged paper background with ink-colored text.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For RTL scripts I'm switching the paper font to Amiri via a <code class="xho5uc7 xlqn4i6 x4p5aij x1j85h84 xf00w7v x1d60ukw x15klxpg x1hjwid2 x1hlhp33">--font-script</code> CSS variable. The right inspector will show shot description, a duration stepper that adjusts the timeline, mood, and sound, plus a regenerate button that cycles through alternate VO lines, with all this state stored per scene in the work object. The timeline itself will render as a horizontal bar with segments flex-sized proportionally to each scene's duration.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Each segment gets labeled with its scene number and shows a selected state, and I'm displaying total runtime against the 60s target with a warning if they diverge. The output view splits into a left side showing a hero still with title, taglines, and export/share buttons (all stubbed with "not connected" toasts), and a right side showing a full ledger of the creative chain from brief through script, with edit links to jump back, followed by the treatment paragraph and next steps.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm designing the directions view, which is heavier: a header, a direction switcher with tabs, and the idea of rendering all three directions as sequential full-width sections so each feels radically distinct, with each section containing a header plus sub-panels for identity, layout philosophy, and more.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Each direction gets five mini panels — identity, layout, navigation model, workspace structure, script experience — built from a shared panel wrapper with theme-specific styling, keeping the wire diagrams lightweight. I'm sketching Direction A as a cinematic noir "title sequence" concept with warm black and vermilion tones, a pipeline-rail navigation, and a three-zone workspace, then starting to define Direction B as "The Specimen" with its own distinct aesthetic.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">And nav as a spatial pinboard with floating clipped ideas, freeform board workspace, and script styled like an annotated manuscript with margin notes.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm leaning toward Direction A, borrowing B's rigor with mono labels and a visible provenance ledger, plus a bit of C's tactile clipping in the Engines stage — it reads immediately as a linear pipeline, suits the cinematic/dark-room feel, handles Arabic serif well, and scales cleanly. Now I'm sketching small theme wireframes, building a generic mini composition function per direction to keep the code compact, starting with a reusable Panel component that takes theme tokens as props.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Sketching the mini renders for each direction: A's nav as a tiny breadcrumb trail with a progress underline, its workspace as three wired columns with a serif-heavy center, its script view as a dark paper sheet with a segmented timeline below, its layout as a 12-column grid with an asymmetric span highlighted, and its identity panel showing swatches, a type specimen, and Arabic script. Now sketching B's nav as a left-side index list.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">C.Script adds manuscript margin notes with italic annotations and mini storyboard squares. Now I'm setting up the font imports and base styles, pulling in distinct typefaces per section to match each direction's character.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Writing theme variables...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Writing theme variables and RTL font overrides...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Good, that resolves correctly since font-sans references the overridden variable on the same element. Now I'm adding the grain overlay with a turbulence SVG background on body::before, plus utility classes like label, field, editable, shimmer, rise, and caret.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now starting the content.ts file, defining language types and the engine ID constants for provocation, analogies, random, opposite, and reversal...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Still writing content types...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also drafting the default brief copy for a fictional client, Dar Coffee Roasters, framing their cold brew launch around an evening ritual rather than morning energy.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">For the objective and constraints, I'm specifying a Riyadh/Jeddah launch campaign targeting late-chronotype creatives, with a warm nocturnal tone and a tight 60-second constraint that forbids showing the product bottle in the first 40 seconds -- a deliberate limitation to force creative reversal.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm sketching the "Provocation" engine: it works by stating something deliberately absurd about the brand and then mining that statement for a usable truth, and I'm testing it with the example that coffee isn't for waking up but for refusing to go to sleep.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Then I move to the "Analogies" engine, which borrows structures from unrelated domains like tides or theatre and maps them onto the brand -- applying it here by comparing cold brew's slow extraction to the slowness of dusk, landing on the idea that cold brew mirrors blue hour: deeper, quieter, and gone before you notice.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Then the "Random Stimulus" engine, forcing a connection between an unrelated object and the brief -- I draw "lighthouse" and trace the links toward guidance and solitary night work, arriving at the insight that late-night work isn't lonely when you have a light to steer by.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Next comes "Opposite Thinking," inverting every assumption in the brief -- not waking people up but keeping them in, not a morning ritual but the city's second morning. Testing which inversions hold true, I land on the idea that evening doesn't mark the day's end in the Gulf but its rebirth, deserving its own drink. Then I move into "Constraint Reversal," treating the limitation itself as the idea.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm pulling together more sharp one-liners, then mapping the surface behavior, hidden tension, and opportunity behind late-night coffee culture in Riyadh. Now I'm starting to draft Route A, "The Second Sunset," built around the idea that the day doesn't end but changes light.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Continuing with Route B, "Last Call for Tomorrow," framed around strangers each one cup away from finishing what they'd put off, then moving into Route C, "The Waiting Hour," which turns the brewing constraint itself into the drama.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm sketching the three brand pillars—nocturnal warmth, slow craft, and quiet confidence—each with a short line explaining it, and starting to draft the opening scene: an exterior shot of the Riyadh skyline at dusk as the city exhales into evening.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Continuing into scene two, Nour closes her laptop in her studio at 7:42pm, hesitating before reopening it with a smile—dialogue hints at "not yet, not here, not tonight"—then moving toward a rooftop night scene where cold brew pours over a single ice sphere, building out each beat with shot type, mood, sound design, and duration.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Closing with the title card: a single amber line drawing into a horizon, the title appearing with "Dar. The second sunset" as the final line, ending on one sustained note then silence — bringing the total to 60 seconds. I'm keeping the title substitution logic separate so the slug stays editable while the actual title renders cleanly in the scene.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm switching to drafting all the Arabic content in Modern Standard Arabic, going through brand labels, navigation, and step names (Brief, Lens, Insight, Concept, Script, Output) with their Arabic equivalents, building out the full bilingual UI string set as I define each key.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Continuing to fill out the remaining copy keys — pipeline labels, lens headings, recent work section, and the four pipeline steps (Brief, Insight, Concept, Script) with their English and Arabic descriptions.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Continuing through the remaining stages, I'm drafting the English copy for engines, insight, and concept — each with its title, description, editable scope, regen action, and next-step label, keeping the tone consistent with the brief stage before moving into the script stage.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm filling in the brief's dynamic trace lines — category, audience signal, and the tension found — alongside a strength meter, then labeling the engine panel (applied to brief, how it thinks, run this lens), the insight panel (generating status, lens, why this works, anatomy scaffold), the concept panel (route, built from insight, title, line, manifesto, principles), and the script panel fields like scenes, runtime, shot, mood, sound, duration, and voiceover.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm rounding out the output panel with export, copy treatment, share board, next creative actions, edit controls, ledger labels, and a toast clarifying this is prototype-only with nothing actually sent. I want the Arabic translations to read naturally rather than feel mechanically translated.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Setting up content.ts...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Still defining more Work fields...</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also thinking through how "Start new brief" should reset state — whether to clear fields entirely or keep a default sample brief so prototyping stays easy, maybe offering a "Load sample" option instead of a fully blank form.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm setting up the App component's top-level state: language, current view, the works object holding both language versions, and toast messaging, with an effect syncing document direction to the current language.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also sketching the routing logic, the view ordering array mapping steps like brief, engines, insight, concept, script, and output, plus a TopBar component that reflects context and current view.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">Now I'm defining shared UI primitives, starting with an Arrow icon that flips direction for RTL layouts and a Btn component with ghost/variant styling, icon support, and flex layout classes.</p>
<p class="xdj266r xvwc6ox x1xtb1vi x1j61x8r x17l0txs xzlkgyw x22v61l x1mzt3pk x1aktaxo xzboxd6">I'm also building a Trace component that reveals lines of text one by one when "live", using a timed effect to progressively increment a counter and animate each line's appearance.</p>
